Id: node-step1x-edit
Title: Step1X-Edit runs without flash-attn, on transformers 5.x
Does: Makes Step1X-Edit run without flash-attn, which it otherwise demands and which has no prebuilt
 wheel for recent CUDA builds -- every Step1X graph failed on import. The same attention runs through
 PyTorch instead. Also fixes its text encoder under current transformers, and finds that encoder in any
 configured models folder rather than one hard-coded path.
Target: custom_nodes/ComfyUI_Step1X-Edit
Source: https://github.com/raykindle/ComfyUI_Step1X-Edit.git
Rev: 1a674089f74f84fd6de8688ea9fbc1a625a34b4a
Why: The pack hard-requires flash-attn, which has no prebuilt wheel for cu13x and will not build
 locally, so every graph died at import. Falling back to PyTorch SDPA when flash_attn_func is absent
 is mathematically equivalent -- the existing "torch" path already does the layout transpose SDPA
 wants. Separately, transformers 5.x moved hidden_size onto config.text_config for Qwen2.5-VL, so the
 embedder read None and allocated a zero-width buffer. The text encoder is located by searching every
 folder ComfyUI configures instead of index [0] of one of them, which is what forced the absolute
 path this was written with -- an install with extra_model_paths.yaml keeps its encoders on a root
 index [0] never looks at. Finally, liger_kernel comes out of requirements.txt: nothing imports it, and
 requiring it drags in triton, which has no Windows wheel, so installing this pack's requirements failed
 outright over a package no code path touches.
